00:28:50.990 --> 00:28:52.010
Come on, boy.

00:28:58.240 --> 00:28:58.640
You...

00:29:00.540 --> 00:29:02.230
What did you do with my uncle?

00:29:02.390 --> 00:29:03.810
Oh, there, there, there.

00:29:04.210 --> 00:29:05.490
Oh, there, there.

00:29:05.590 --> 00:29:06.070
Let me go.

00:29:06.570 --> 00:29:07.250
There, there.

00:29:07.530 --> 00:29:07.770
Quiet.

00:29:08.310 --> 00:29:09.060
Let me go.

00:29:09.740 --> 00:29:10.220
Please.

00:29:10.540 --> 00:29:12.700
It's a strange thing about these headphones.

00:29:13.710 --> 00:29:17.010
One never knows what hallucinations they will produce.

00:29:17.850 --> 00:29:18.970
I'll quiet him.

00:29:19.070 --> 00:29:19.250
No.

00:29:19.670 --> 00:29:19.930
Please.

00:29:20.250 --> 00:29:20.670
Let me go.

00:29:20.670 --> 00:29:21.030
I'll tell you.

00:29:21.510 --> 00:29:23.190
May I ask you to help me?

00:29:23.750 --> 00:29:25.910
Now, push down the sleeve.

00:29:26.810 --> 00:29:27.410
When down.

00:29:28.010 --> 00:29:28.270
There.

00:29:28.800 --> 00:29:29.160
Please.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:31.590
Please, don't let him touch me.

00:29:31.820 --> 00:29:33.260
Try to understand, it's the doctor.

00:29:33.560 --> 00:29:36.020
No, no, I tell you, it's Carl.

00:29:37.460 --> 00:29:40.990
There now, hold him tight now.

00:29:41.770 --> 00:29:42.770
Hey, wait a minute, stop.

00:29:42.990 --> 00:29:44.130
What nonsense is this?

00:29:44.150 --> 00:29:44.610
No, no.

00:29:44.980 --> 00:29:46.760
I wouldn't get there with a doctor, miss.

00:29:47.140 --> 00:29:47.920
Let her alone.

00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:48.220
Hold him.

00:29:48.220 --> 00:29:48.680
Take your hand off her.

00:29:48.680 --> 00:29:49.100
Hold him.

00:29:49.320 --> 00:29:49.900
Drop that.

00:29:50.180 --> 00:29:50.360
Quick.

00:29:50.360 --> 00:29:50.640
Quick.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:04.640
You have a positive genius for being just in time, Mr. Kent.

00:30:04.640 --> 00:30:05.640
Don't stop to talk.

00:30:05.640 --> 00:30:06.670
Take me to Prince Evan.

00:30:06.670 --> 00:30:08.900
And if I should refuse?

00:30:08.900 --> 00:30:09.900
Quick!

00:30:09.900 --> 00:30:11.850
Get it!

00:30:11.850 --> 00:30:16.650
Lights!

00:30:16.650 --> 00:30:19.310
Lights!

00:30:19.310 --> 00:30:22.350
Lights!

00:30:22.350 --> 00:30:23.890
Quick!

00:30:23.890 --> 00:30:25.610
I saw a shadow.

00:30:25.610 --> 00:30:26.610
Go by me.

00:30:26.610 --> 00:30:27.610
Where'd they go?

00:30:27.610 --> 00:30:28.620
Where are they?

00:30:28.620 --> 00:30:29.620
Did you see them?

00:30:29.620 --> 00:30:30.000
They were not there.

00:31:07.260 --> 00:31:07.860
Steve Hahn.

00:31:11.430 --> 00:31:13.470
Oh, I've killed him.

00:31:14.290 --> 00:31:16.200
No, no, you didn't kill him.

00:31:17.010 --> 00:31:18.290
He's been dead for some time.

00:31:19.110 --> 00:31:19.650
Are you sure?

00:31:20.300 --> 00:31:21.630
Look at his throat.

00:31:25.150 --> 00:31:26.830
Well, there's no sign of him in there.

00:31:28.380 --> 00:31:29.640
Home Kennedy send more men.

00:31:35.340 --> 00:31:36.280
Excuse me, please.

00:31:36.360 --> 00:31:36.520
Brett.

00:31:36.800 --> 00:31:37.080
Brett.

00:31:37.240 --> 00:31:40.260
When you get Kennedy on the phone, tell him I want a dragnet thrown around this district.

00:31:40.400 --> 00:31:40.900
Yes, sir.

00:31:41.310 --> 00:31:43.570
And Brett, while you're about it, you might as well telephone me here.

00:31:44.030 --> 00:31:46.520
Such hanky-panky at 2 o'clock in the morning.

00:31:46.780 --> 00:31:48.980
Everybody tramping around, stepping all over people.

00:31:51.830 --> 00:31:55.100
Two boys have got to get out of here at once.

00:31:55.360 --> 00:31:56.180
Where can we go?

00:31:56.300 --> 00:31:57.260
Well, I'm hanged if I know.

00:31:57.650 --> 00:31:59.520
I wish I knew someplace outside of town.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:05.260
feel you were safe. I know. Aunt Abby's house. Where's that? It's way off in the country.

00:32:05.740 --> 00:32:11.560
They'd never find it. Well, that might be just the place to lie low for a few days. Not

00:32:11.560 --> 00:32:16.880
me. I don't leave here until we get Carl. Oh, now look here, my boy. You've got to realize

00:32:16.880 --> 00:32:21.520
we're dealing with a madman. Let me run things. So long as you're here, my hands are tied.

00:32:21.740 --> 00:32:25.790
But with you safely out of the way... Please. Please do as he says. Nick, Nick, don't be

00:32:25.790 --> 00:32:30.000
a fool. We've got to get away from here. All right, I'll go. Yes.

00:32:30.120 --> 00:32:30.980
Now, then that's settled.

00:32:31.340 --> 00:32:34.420
Now, I've got a plan for smuggling you out of the house so that no one will know.

00:32:34.830 --> 00:32:37.510
I'll bring my car around the street a block from here.

00:32:44.420 --> 00:32:47.850
Well, all I've got to say is, if I was running the United States,

00:32:48.130 --> 00:32:49.150
it's too pearl to.

00:32:50.200 --> 00:32:51.960
That carloff would never have been let into the country.

00:32:52.640 --> 00:32:53.660
It's too pearl to.

00:32:54.720 --> 00:32:57.280
Makes oysters run up and down my spine to think he's still loose.

00:33:18.110 --> 00:33:21.950
It was irreceivable to me how he could get away with both the police and Secret Service after him.

00:33:23.830 --> 00:33:28.280
What's that?

00:33:28.750 --> 00:33:29.680
It's at the front door.

00:33:40.110 --> 00:33:41.290
You want me to open it, sir?

00:33:42.260 --> 00:33:43.620
Yes, but have your gun handy.

00:33:49.420 --> 00:33:57.270
I just came from headquarters with a message from Mr. Kent.

00:33:57.410 --> 00:33:57.710
Oh.

00:33:58.220 --> 00:33:58.650
Come in.

00:34:02.270 --> 00:34:03.610
It's a message from headquarters.

00:34:04.380 --> 00:34:05.200
Mr. Bob Karloff?

00:34:06.020 --> 00:34:07.200
Karloff is dead, sir.

00:34:08.090 --> 00:34:08.410
Dead?

00:34:08.810 --> 00:34:09.360
Yes, sir.

00:34:10.330 --> 00:34:11.000
Here's a letter.

00:34:12.170 --> 00:34:13.910
Oh, now you're safe.

00:34:14.980 --> 00:34:17.140
Well, bless Providence, now we can sleep nights.

00:34:19.360 --> 00:34:21.520
Does it really say Karloff's dead, Mr. Kent?

00:34:21.680 --> 00:34:21.980
Yes.

00:34:23.140 --> 00:34:24.920
One of his men betrayed his hiding place.

00:34:25.220 --> 00:34:28.960
Before the police could break in, he committed suicide by exploding a bomb.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.580
I want you to come up and identify the body, sir.

00:34:31.900 --> 00:34:32.750
I brought down a car.

00:34:33.330 --> 00:34:33.790
Oh, I see.

00:34:34.470 --> 00:34:36.240
You're a new man, aren't you?

00:34:36.500 --> 00:34:37.790
I don't remember seeing you before.

00:34:38.210 --> 00:34:39.370
I've been working on the West Coast.

00:34:39.470 --> 00:34:39.630
Oh.

00:34:40.010 --> 00:34:41.020
If you want to see my credentials...

00:34:41.020 --> 00:34:41.860
No, no, no, no, no.

00:34:41.920 --> 00:34:42.760
This letter's in code.

00:34:43.140 --> 00:34:43.620
I'll go with you.

00:34:48.860 --> 00:34:51.890
I don't like his looks.

00:34:52.350 --> 00:34:53.030
You think it's safe?

00:34:53.840 --> 00:34:54.360
Now, don't worry.

00:34:54.870 --> 00:34:55.450
Trust me.

00:34:55.980 --> 00:34:56.960
Everything will be all right.

00:35:06.810 --> 00:35:15.330
Now listen, get this straight, right sir.

00:35:37.390 --> 00:35:38.030
Where's your car?

00:35:38.660 --> 00:35:40.120
Down the road by that old mill.

00:35:41.350 --> 00:35:42.340
Come on.

00:35:50.500 --> 00:35:56.600
Well, that's a relief.

00:36:04.800 --> 00:36:08.560
How you folks feel, but all this gallivans made me hungry.

00:36:08.960 --> 00:36:10.340
I'm going to fix us a bang-up dinner.

00:36:10.880 --> 00:36:11.240
Hooray!

00:36:11.900 --> 00:36:15.200
Hey, Prince, you trot down cell and fetch me up a bucket of coal.

00:36:16.110 --> 00:36:16.910
You mean me?

00:36:17.290 --> 00:36:18.090
Yes, you.

00:36:18.600 --> 00:36:20.570
It won't hurt you to saw your hands for once.

00:36:22.560 --> 00:36:23.080
Very well.

00:36:23.520 --> 00:36:24.040
Where is it?

00:36:24.600 --> 00:36:25.780
Second door to the left.

00:36:26.590 --> 00:36:27.930
And shake up the furnace for you now.

00:36:30.160 --> 00:36:33.060
I'm sorry to speak ill of your kin, but I don't like his face.

00:36:33.340 --> 00:36:34.000
Aunt Abby!

00:36:34.200 --> 00:36:35.900
Don't you want to have me, Kitty Conover?

00:36:36.260 --> 00:36:39.560
He's a spitting image of that fellow who sold me stocking a diamond mine last spring.

00:36:40.230 --> 00:36:42.130
You don't see me wearing any diamonds, do you?

00:36:43.690 --> 00:36:44.330
Don't go.

00:36:45.070 --> 00:36:48.430
I want to tell you what a trump I think you were for trusting me last night.

00:36:48.710 --> 00:36:49.810
I didn't trust you.

00:36:50.170 --> 00:36:51.770
I had you covered all the time.

00:36:57.360 --> 00:36:57.940
Oh.

00:37:00.800 --> 00:37:03.040
- Do you like American music?

00:37:03.040 --> 00:37:04.200
- And American girls.

00:37:05.460 --> 00:37:06.930
My mother was an American.

00:37:06.930 --> 00:37:11.600
My father met her over here and fell in love with it.

00:37:11.600 --> 00:37:12.910
It runs in the family.

00:37:21.150 --> 00:37:22.880
I like American weddings, too.

00:37:53.320 --> 00:37:58.430
- Good evening, Mr. Kent, doctor.

00:37:58.430 --> 00:37:59.960
- Good evening, Mr. Kent.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:00.740
Good evening, Doctor.

00:38:01.300 --> 00:38:04.360
I see the reports of your death have been considerably exaggerated.

00:38:05.560 --> 00:38:06.120
Considerably?

00:38:06.760 --> 00:38:10.580
I suppose it was the traitor who was found dead in your place.

00:38:10.890 --> 00:38:11.270
Right.

00:38:11.820 --> 00:38:15.620
Just before the bomb exploded, I changed clothes with him

00:38:15.620 --> 00:38:19.120
and escaped under the very noses of your men.

00:38:20.290 --> 00:38:22.790
If you're not afraid to try one.

00:38:22.910 --> 00:38:24.290
Oh, no, not at all.

00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:28.370
I don't believe you'd be so unoriginal as to...

00:38:28.370 --> 00:38:30.000
Oh, no, no, no.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:37.460
I don't need to ask how your man got hold of that letter from headquarters.

00:38:37.460 --> 00:38:44.480
No. I fancy it's quite obvious. The body of their messenger ought to show up at the

00:38:44.480 --> 00:38:51.960
top of the mill pond in, say, four or five days. I figured the code letter would keep

00:38:51.960 --> 00:39:00.000
you from suspecting my man. But still, I'm disappointed in you, Mr. Kent. I didn't think you would walk

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:07.080
into my trap quite so blindly. Would it make you any happier to know I saw the trap and

00:39:07.080 --> 00:39:13.620
walked into it deliberately? When I heard the body was unrecognizable, I knew you were

00:39:13.620 --> 00:39:20.620
still alive, and in hopes of preventing further killings, I let your man lead me to you so

00:39:20.620 --> 00:39:21.760
that I could do this.

00:39:30.910 --> 00:39:32.600
All of them over the heart.

00:39:33.820 --> 00:39:39.420
But fortunately, in Russia, I acquired the habit of wearing a bulletproof vest.

00:39:40.780 --> 00:39:43.540
Peter, we searched him, sir.

00:39:43.800 --> 00:39:45.180
He took my revolver away.

00:39:45.650 --> 00:39:47.060
I had the second one hidden.

00:39:47.640 --> 00:39:48.650
Very clever.

00:39:51.400 --> 00:39:59.240
But didn't it occur to you that you might fail and that the consequences would not be pleasant?

00:39:59.600 --> 00:40:00.000
Naturally.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:05.470
You should have been a Russian, Mr. Kent.

00:40:05.470 --> 00:40:07.900
You would have been a great help to me.

00:40:07.900 --> 00:40:08.850
Hardly.

00:40:08.850 --> 00:40:11.410
You see, I consider you a madman.

00:40:11.410 --> 00:40:13.780
Because I kill people?

00:40:13.780 --> 00:40:16.690
Yesterday you killed my man.

00:40:16.690 --> 00:40:19.380
Just now you try to kill me.

00:40:19.380 --> 00:40:23.180
Do you consider yourself a madman?

00:40:23.180 --> 00:40:28.810
Take him upstairs.

00:40:34.540 --> 00:40:37.160
A little formula I'm preparing.

00:40:37.950 --> 00:40:38.450
For me?

00:40:39.220 --> 00:40:39.700
Oh, no.

00:40:40.120 --> 00:40:41.490
I can't spare you.

00:40:42.230 --> 00:40:42.850
Not yet.

00:40:43.660 --> 00:40:44.580
You amuse me.

00:40:45.130 --> 00:40:47.790
In fact, you are my trump card.

00:40:48.620 --> 00:40:52.210
Watch him carefully and see that he does not escape.

00:40:52.750 --> 00:40:53.370
Yes, doctor.

00:40:56.270 --> 00:40:58.190
Oh, Mr. Kent.

00:40:59.010 --> 00:41:00.000
I mostly...

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:02.970
rudely, omitted to answer your question.

00:41:04.210 --> 00:41:06.470
I am brewing this for the Petrogs.

00:41:07.020 --> 00:41:10.260
By the time it is ready, they will be here.

00:41:14.590 --> 00:41:17.540
Mr. Mike Moore of the White Lake, Your Highness.

00:41:18.030 --> 00:41:19.650
No, thank you. I've had two helpinges already.

00:41:19.870 --> 00:41:20.690
I'll take another piece.

00:41:21.860 --> 00:41:22.580
You would.

00:41:34.510 --> 00:41:40.110
merciful goodness. Certainly is a bad storm blowing up. Well, I wish you wouldn't make

00:41:40.110 --> 00:41:45.710
so much fuss about it. I never did see that lightning did anybody any good, except lightning

00:41:45.710 --> 00:42:00.000
rod salesman. Only the wind. I saw a man's face out there. Oh, I did.

00:42:02.330 --> 00:42:02.990
Wait, I'll see.

00:42:03.320 --> 00:42:03.620
Wait.

00:42:07.400 --> 00:42:11.060
You mustn't go out there, sir.

00:42:11.440 --> 00:42:12.980
Mr. Kent left positive orders.

00:42:13.350 --> 00:42:14.210
Oh, that's nonsense.

00:42:14.670 --> 00:42:15.850
There isn't any danger there now.

00:42:16.290 --> 00:42:16.950
Karloff is dead.

00:42:17.870 --> 00:42:18.530
You wait here.

00:42:18.590 --> 00:42:19.310
I'll go and see.

00:42:21.920 --> 00:42:28.900
Someone has been here.

00:42:32.040 --> 00:42:32.640
Put on the light.

00:42:32.900 --> 00:42:33.420
Where are they?

00:42:33.600 --> 00:42:34.440
Over there in the corner.

00:42:35.760 --> 00:42:36.620
It's work.

00:42:39.600 --> 00:42:40.140
Here's the match.

00:42:46.210 --> 00:42:47.630
Where is Brett?

00:42:47.850 --> 00:42:49.230
He must be out there.

00:42:49.550 --> 00:42:49.810
Brett.

00:42:50.030 --> 00:42:50.250
Brett.

00:42:50.900 --> 00:42:51.340
Oh, Brett.

00:42:53.620 --> 00:42:54.160
Wait, listen.

00:42:55.570 --> 00:42:57.490
There's someone at the front door.

00:42:58.870 --> 00:42:59.400
I'll go.

00:43:16.960 --> 00:43:19.040
- He's dead?

00:43:19.040 --> 00:43:20.260
- Okay, get him over there, quick.

00:43:30.190 --> 00:43:31.070
They got me.

00:43:31.780 --> 00:43:33.880
Carl is alive.

00:43:37.390 --> 00:43:41.140
What's this?

00:43:48.340 --> 00:43:49.700
It's addressed to you.

00:44:20.760 --> 00:44:22.080
I'm going to phone the sheriff.

00:44:30.220 --> 00:44:30.520
Hello?

00:44:30.930 --> 00:44:43.330
Hello!

00:44:43.940 --> 00:44:47.790
Anybody?

00:44:49.050 --> 00:44:49.980
Hello?

00:44:50.890 --> 00:44:52.590
What's wrong?

00:44:52.670 --> 00:44:54.170
I can't get anyone.

00:44:54.550 --> 00:44:55.070
Let me try.

00:44:57.450 --> 00:44:57.650
Hello.

00:44:58.620 --> 00:44:58.840
Hello.

00:45:00.060 --> 00:45:00.420
Hello.

00:45:07.070 --> 00:45:07.890
They've cut the line.

00:45:08.670 --> 00:45:09.670
Kitty Conover, come with me.

00:45:09.730 --> 00:45:10.570
We'll get some more candles.

00:45:10.910 --> 00:45:12.710
One thing we're going to have is plenty of light.

00:45:15.250 --> 00:45:15.590
Gregor.

00:45:18.260 --> 00:45:19.220
Gregor.

00:45:20.950 --> 00:45:22.750
Do you know what this means?

00:45:23.600 --> 00:45:24.380
Karloff is alive.

00:45:24.720 --> 00:45:25.740
There's only one thing for us to do.

00:45:26.130 --> 00:45:27.510
You and I have got to get out of this house.

00:45:28.130 --> 00:45:29.030
Out of this house?

00:45:29.170 --> 00:45:29.490
Yes.

00:45:30.440 --> 00:45:32.520
As long as we stay here, we're endangering the women.

00:45:33.050 --> 00:45:34.290
But we can't go out.

00:45:35.050 --> 00:45:35.970
Karloff will kill us.

00:45:36.210 --> 00:45:38.220
Well, we can give him a run for his money.

00:45:39.380 --> 00:45:40.640
Well, you can go if you want to.

00:45:41.090 --> 00:45:42.770
But I'm staying here.

00:45:43.030 --> 00:45:43.830
But listen, Gregor.

00:45:44.120 --> 00:45:45.550
I'm staying here.

00:45:45.790 --> 00:45:46.110
Please.

00:45:46.150 --> 00:45:46.410
Wait.

00:45:46.900 --> 00:45:47.540
He's right.

00:45:47.900 --> 00:45:49.390
You can't leave this house tonight.

00:45:49.790 --> 00:45:50.790
You must be sensible.

00:45:51.420 --> 00:45:52.560
Karloff has no quarrel with you.

00:45:52.560 --> 00:45:54.320
If we leave here, he'll let you alone.

00:45:54.890 --> 00:45:56.790
All he wants is Gregor and me.

00:46:47.500 --> 00:46:48.060
Where are you going?

00:46:48.300 --> 00:46:49.000
To get the sheriff.

00:46:49.590 --> 00:46:52.870
When it comes to killing men all over my front steps, he's got to put a stop to it.

00:46:53.160 --> 00:46:54.120
But they'll catch you.

00:46:54.320 --> 00:46:58.520
Well, if they do, least ways I'll have the comfort of giving the Russians a piece of my mind.

00:46:58.760 --> 00:46:59.060
Wait.

00:47:05.150 --> 00:47:15.870
case Karloff should get you. I've got a message. I've been wondering how to get it to him. I'm

00:47:15.870 --> 00:47:22.680
offering to give myself up if he let the rest of you go. Well, now that's real noble of

00:47:22.680 --> 00:47:30.000
you, Prince. Maybe I've been a little hasty. You aren't so bad. Here, we'll talk to you.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:32.120
some more when I get back with the sheriff.

00:48:00.570 --> 00:48:01.410
Nicholas, please.

00:48:01.610 --> 00:48:02.490
There's no use arguing.

00:48:02.930 --> 00:48:03.570
Gregor and I are leaving.

00:48:03.900 --> 00:48:05.370
But I don't want you to go.

00:48:05.760 --> 00:48:08.560
I'm sorry, but...

00:48:08.560 --> 00:48:08.860
Gregor?

00:48:10.690 --> 00:48:12.140
Gregor?

00:48:13.150 --> 00:48:14.610
I wonder where he is.

00:48:20.170 --> 00:48:20.590
Gregor?

00:48:23.340 --> 00:48:23.820
Gregor?

00:48:24.780 --> 00:48:25.520
Aunt Abby?

00:48:26.260 --> 00:48:27.450
Aunt Abby?

00:48:27.450 --> 00:48:27.810
Aunt Abby?

00:48:30.160 --> 00:48:39.890
wonder where they are. I don't know. Maybe they're upstairs. Well, let's go and see.

00:49:05.400 --> 00:49:08.980
Well, the fellow actually offers to trust my word.

00:49:10.140 --> 00:49:12.200
A rat caught in a trap has no choice.

00:49:13.390 --> 00:49:14.250
Very true.

00:49:16.370 --> 00:49:16.850
Bring him.

00:49:17.880 --> 00:49:20.470
I have a use for rats.

00:49:22.170 --> 00:49:23.280
I will bring him.

00:49:30.640 --> 00:49:31.580
Now we'll talk.

00:49:32.150 --> 00:49:33.530
I do not doubt it, madam.

00:49:34.040 --> 00:49:36.200
I've been waiting to get at you for a long time.

00:49:36.340 --> 00:49:37.760
I'm flattered, Miss Cramp.

00:49:37.820 --> 00:49:39.120
Well, you won't be so flattered.

00:49:39.500 --> 00:49:40.980
You'll be flattened when I get through.

00:49:41.640 --> 00:49:43.440
I've been itching to give you a piece of my mind.

00:49:43.460 --> 00:49:44.180
But, my dear...

00:49:44.180 --> 00:49:45.420
Now, don't you try to talk,

00:49:45.460 --> 00:49:47.620
because it won't do you mighty good till I've had my say.

00:49:48.660 --> 00:49:49.900
I know your sort.

00:49:50.290 --> 00:49:51.530
Making jokes about everything.

00:49:51.850 --> 00:49:52.470
Even murder.

00:49:53.230 --> 00:49:55.630
I've seen them born, and I've seen them grow up.

00:49:56.030 --> 00:49:58.030
Pulling wings off flies when they're babies.

00:49:59.040 --> 00:50:00.000
Hunting robins.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:04.800
with slingshots and drowning tomcats when they're boys, shooting and murdering when

00:50:04.800 --> 00:50:11.630
they're men. And where are they now? I ask you, where are they now? Why, I'm sure I don't

00:50:11.630 --> 00:50:19.720
know. Where are they? Hung. That's what. Every mother son of them. Hung. Doctor, Prince

00:50:19.720 --> 00:50:25.000
Gregor is out of line. And mark my word, my man. Take this woman away. She annoys me.

00:50:25.000 --> 00:50:30.000
You will end on a scaffold yourself with your salivars and your vodkas and all

00:50:34.410 --> 00:50:42.710
say is i never did like caviar russian dancers squatting down on their hind legs running a mile

00:50:42.710 --> 00:50:52.650
and getting nowhere take your hands off me you sneaky samovar for you you vulgar

00:50:52.650 --> 00:51:00.000
you say it is your brother and

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:09.310
Nicholas, who killed my daughter. Yes. And I'll show you a way to get him if you let me go. You

00:51:09.310 --> 00:51:18.170
haven't anything against me now, have you? I swear, it wasn't I. There's no need to swear. My daughter

00:51:18.170 --> 00:51:30.000
could never have cared for a thing like you. I have seen men die by the thousand. I've seen them shot

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:37.020
against walls, stabbed with bayonets. But never have I seen a man low enough to betray his own

00:51:37.020 --> 00:51:47.110
brother to save his filthy hide. I'm not betraying him. I tell you, he did it. He did it.

00:51:47.420 --> 00:51:53.180
I promised you wouldn't touch me. I don't intend to touch your highness. I wish to

00:51:53.180 --> 00:52:00.000
make a little experiment. I am not certain that this formula is correct. And I need a

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:01.620
rack to try it on.

00:52:02.460 --> 00:52:02.900
Get him.

00:52:03.160 --> 00:52:03.740
Oh, no.

00:52:04.580 --> 00:52:06.320
Oh, I want to be home.

00:52:07.240 --> 00:52:07.500
Oh.

00:52:07.700 --> 00:52:08.120
In here.

00:52:09.390 --> 00:52:10.470
I want to be honest.

00:52:11.030 --> 00:52:12.260
I promise you wouldn't touch me now.

00:52:12.740 --> 00:52:14.180
Now, help me.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:32.000
Let me out, let me out!

00:52:32.000 --> 00:52:33.890
I didn't, I swear I didn't do it!

00:52:33.890 --> 00:52:36.150
No! No, Carlos, not that!

00:52:36.150 --> 00:52:37.100
No!

00:52:37.100 --> 00:53:00.000
The formula seems to be quite correct.

00:53:02.520 --> 00:53:06.370
Remove the body and clear the room of gas.

00:53:07.670 --> 00:53:08.890
We shall need it again.

00:53:13.240 --> 00:53:29.960
What is this?

00:53:30.730 --> 00:53:31.640
Dora.

00:53:31.640 --> 00:53:44.980
Dresslinger's dummy.

00:54:39.280 --> 00:54:40.540
I wonder what's happened to them.

00:54:41.000 --> 00:54:42.160
I can't figure it out.

00:55:30.600 --> 00:55:35.540
Oh, this room is as cold as the grave.

00:55:35.540 --> 00:55:39.400
I trust your highness won't find it unhealthy.

00:55:39.400 --> 00:55:42.570
I don't suppose I'll have time to catch cold.

00:55:42.570 --> 00:55:47.120
No, this is not for you.

00:55:47.120 --> 00:55:51.780
It's for Miss Conover.

00:55:51.780 --> 00:55:53.260
Miss Conover?

00:55:53.260 --> 00:55:55.970
You're not going to hurt her.

00:55:55.970 --> 00:55:56.970
Oh, no.

00:55:56.970 --> 00:56:00.000
You are to use...

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:09.540
this night. Why do you think that I was... You killed my daughter, whom I loved. Now I am going

00:56:09.540 --> 00:56:17.770
to watch you kill the woman you love. I didn't kill your daughter. For my word. I've already

00:56:17.770 --> 00:56:30.000
had the word of a Petrov that you did. Your finest Prince Gregor betrayed you to me.

00:56:30.920 --> 00:56:32.710
Just before he dies.

00:56:36.510 --> 00:56:42.730
You will need your hand.

00:57:03.960 --> 00:57:05.960
You know, you can't force me to do that.

00:57:05.960 --> 00:57:08.100
It is your choice, Phoenix.

00:57:08.100 --> 00:57:14.820
But let me remind you that after your death, she will be in our hands alone.

00:57:42.800 --> 00:57:46.020
I will give you as long as that candle burn.

00:57:46.020 --> 00:57:52.660
That ought to be time enough for a very crispy love scene.

00:58:12.700 --> 00:58:16.120
Remember, the candle is burning at both ends.

00:58:40.810 --> 00:58:42.640
Why did Karloff leave this night?

00:59:01.690 --> 00:59:04.370
Bring in Mr. Kent and that woman.

00:59:46.030 --> 00:59:47.030
What are you going to do?

00:59:47.030 --> 00:59:49.520
These stones are loose.

00:59:49.520 --> 00:59:52.120
Maybe we can dig our way out.

01:00:13.050 --> 01:00:18.690
up let's be pleased to know that your imprisonment is at an end. You mean you're letting us go?

01:00:18.870 --> 01:00:25.460
I do. How about Kitty and that young pet lock? When I'm safely away from here, you may remove

01:00:25.460 --> 01:00:30.000
their bodies. You mean... They're dead? No. Not dead?

01:00:31.410 --> 01:00:33.310
But he will not have long to wait.

01:00:39.240 --> 01:00:48.680
Something else in there.

01:00:51.900 --> 01:00:54.820
Maybe I can break through it.

01:00:57.180 --> 01:01:00.000
You expect him to kill that?

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:01.060
Girl, no.

01:01:01.850 --> 01:01:04.550
